WEBVTT

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.420
Fight!

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.490
"Heroes are Born"

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:04.130
Team Rabbits of the MJP,

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:08.240
in recognition of your
remarkable feat at Undina Base,

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.610
we award you the Level-3
Order of Merit Medal.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:30.780
The acting head of the Pacific
Rim-India Alliance presented

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.380
medals to members of the MJP.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.040
They earned that?!

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.670
For real?

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.420
The young heroes obtained our

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.410
first major victory since the

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.590
Global Defense Force began
fighting the Wulgaru.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.890
It was their first
time in actual combat.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.520
They defended Undina Base,
which we were going to

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.420
abandon, and forced the elite
Wulgaru fleet to retreat.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.180
Dang, I'm glad we established the MJP.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.640
As a member of

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.200
the Pacific Rim-India Alliance,
I'm proud we did, Commander Simon.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:06.240
At any rate, this organization
is finally beginning to bear fruit.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.500
It's hard to believe we've been

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.050
fighting in space development
equipment thus far.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.840
I'm not sure I'd say it is
"bearing fruit" after one victory,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.510
let alone one that was a fluke.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.410
It's too soon to tell if
it's worth the expense.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.300
Indeed.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.470
The MJP needed a massive budget
to create children who can fight.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.470
Created to fight, these
children were stripped

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:31.770
of their lives the moment they were born.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.900
I find it lamentable.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.750
Intelligence Strategist Amane!

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:41.980
The MJP was a project created to
adapt humans to life in outer space,

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.110
not to pump out soldiers
with no purpose but to fight.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.880
Lt. Amane, refrain from making
such thoughtless remarks.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.510
The MJP is currently the center of attention.
It could create misconceptions.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:56.900
Very well.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.360
I'll tell the commander
about the press conference.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:01.320
I am terribly sorry, but we're swamped
with requests for interviews.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:05.140
I hate to say it, but we cannot
give you one anytime soon.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.270
I bet they're hounding
Undina Base as well!

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.230
Now then, please present
your questions one at a time.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.360
Uh, I'd like to go first.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.200
What exactly are you?

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:24.950
What were those machines?

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.450
Are they the GDF's secret weapons?

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:34.150
They are students currently enrolled in
the Gurantseere Cosmopolitan Academy.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.760
Students? They're students?

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:36.460
They are affiliated with
the secret service, MJP.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.570
What does MJP stand for?

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.930
Military Junior Pre-Academy.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:43.370
It's an organization that trains
future military officers.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:48.060
The AHSMB units they pilot
use the GDF's cutting-edge frames,

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.140
but I cannot discuss them in detail.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:54.420
Uh, then I have another question
for everyone in the MJP.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.280
How did you feel when you were ordered
to fight in that mission?

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:00.150
Right. It was a true honor to...

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.180
Asagi? What's wrong?

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.590
My stomach... It's the stress.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:06.610
Anyone else?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.030
I felt the same.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:10.600
Tamaki.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.330
That was a huge hit, Tamaki!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.000
Too cute
It went 'Bang!'
That noise hurt
Aha ha ha ha

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.000
Was she trying to be cute?
Juggle failed
What's with these guys?
Nice head shot!

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.970
Wow, these comments rock!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.710
Suruga, answer the question!

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.280
You, too.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.610
Ow!

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:26.550
Are you all right?

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.510
What was the key point
behind this mission?

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.650
Kei, please answer that.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.180
I can't.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.350
Then I will!

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:36.430
My unit's primary guns are a 90 mm
L/70 high-energy charged particle cannon

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.320
and two 40mm L/45 radiation-guided

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.010
photon resonance antiaircraft
cannons as its co-ax guns.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:43.120
I can catch any enemies in range
with a Type 99 high-depth, 3D,

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.400
inversed spectroscopic rangefinder
manufactured by Imperial Japan Optics Meter.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.230
Then I use the co-ax...

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:49.400
Uh, allow me to change the question.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.150
Didn't the plan originally
call for you to pull back?

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.010
Correct.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.580
So who decided to change the plan?

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.180
Izuru...

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.950
Uh, Second Lieutenant Izuru Hitachi.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:02.550
Second Lt. Hitachi,

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.220
is it true that you decided to fight

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.210
to the end once you learned that
civilians were still there?

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:09.430
What was running through your mind?

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.700
Uh, well...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.440
Uh, what is that...?

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.360
This is the hero in a story I'm writing.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.420
In other words, this is how I felt.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.280
Aw, jeez!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.950
Thinks he's a big shot.
Weird illo
I was like him once.
Total moron                                       Moron
He sucks!                    Not good, not bad...
He's special...
What is he going for?

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:36.870
Uh, please tell us what
your favorite food is.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:37.560
Curry!

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.330
Do you have a boyfriend?
Curry!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.130
I'm accepting applications!

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.530
Accepting applications!
Accepting applications!                              AWESOME!!!
Accepting applications!       This is-LOLOL
Cute!
Laughed so hard I... LOLOLOL            HOT!
Accepting applications!                        ROFLOL
WOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO
LOL
Accepting applications!

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.290
Accepting applications!     I'll be your BF!
You're too-LOLOLOL
SHE'S CUTELOLOLOL
Spaz
Cute!Not me
Hot!                    Breasts! Breasts!
I'll become your boyfriend!            Hmm~~
Accepting applications!
Annoying!

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:46.710
I am sorry, but they cannot answer
questions about their private lives.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.720
They are extremely tired,
so we are going to call it a-

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.570
Then let us take some pictures

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:55.580
of them with the base as
the backdrop, Miss Manager.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:57.560
"Manager"?

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:06.820
Thank you!

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:08.100
Thank you!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.170
Thank you very much!

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.380
Are these the people we saved?

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:28.710
Wow...

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:30.570
Tearing up?

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.640
Awesome!

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:41.710
I'm beat...

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.150
Now I can finally relax.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.230
My stomach hurts.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.660
We're all over the news.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.250
There's our school!

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.470
Stop watching that!

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.650
You're making
my stomachache worse.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:53.270
Here.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:57.660
It's my job as leader.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:01.680
This isn't the sort of
thing a leader does.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.880
Isn't it great how everyone survived?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.050
I thought you were
going to get me killed.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.690
We're lucky things turned
out like they did.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.470
You stupy-dupy dude!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.090
And what the heck is up with this?

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.010
The heroes who saved Earth!
The Majestic Princes

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:17.170
Heroes...

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.070
They're calling us the
"Majestic Princes".

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:22.080
But why?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.650
Probably because we're in the MJP.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:25.640
Why must they call us that?

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.310
I'm not a prince.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.290
Be quiet!

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.230
The world is filled with too much noise.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.780
But, dang! Izuru, you
were awesome back there.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.140
Yeah, you seemed like a
totally different person.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.450
Do you think I transformed?

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:42.720
Come again?

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:43.930
Into a hero.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:44.750
Of course not!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.750
But we were different, too.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.870
Wasn't it kinda weird?

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.960
Yeah. It felt like
some strange power was

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.230
building up inside me
when I was in my AHSMB.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:54.760
That was the JURIA-SYSTEM.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:01.710
The JURIA-SYSTEM was
built around your DNA.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.400
DNA does whatever it can to survive.

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:08.020
As such, it has strong
survival instinct.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:12.690
That survival instinct is what made your
AHSMB units try to flee at first.

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:16.740
But it becomes extremely offensive
when your fighting instinct surges.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:20.450
Consequentially, AHSMB will act on its own
and run independent of you.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.910
So when it selected that weapon
without any commands...

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.050
That was the JURIA-SYSTEM's doing.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.380
You could say the performance exhibited by
an AHSMB with heightened fighting instinct

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:33.430
is akin to when a person exhibits feats of
adrenaline-fueled hysterical strength.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.610
As a result, they push their limits,
causing them to break down frequently.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:41.100
The JURIA-SYSTEM
has the fight-or-flight instinct.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.900
As pilots, you must control
both forms of survival instinct.

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:49.910
In other words, you must
tame a wild stallion.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.860
There you have it. Did you get all that?

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.290
Yes...

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.320
That is the extent of my explanation.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:57.280
Team Rabbits, I order you to remobilize.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.240
I want you to set up the destroyed
transmission satellites' replacements.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:04.910
Now then, about your AHSMB units...

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:07.930
What happened to them?!

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.540
After seeing your performance,

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.250
we've had a group of sponsors
offer financial backing.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:16.560
What the hell?!

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:20.160
I take that brand of antacid.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.500
That's messed up...

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:23.590
What is with these ads?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.000
There's my grill...

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.020
A camera will be there
to gather footage,

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:32.030
so do your best to make sure
it can see those logos.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:35.050
We aren't some freak show!

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.630
We have to do this to spread
the word about the MJP.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:39.660
Roger that!

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:43.960
So, would it be all right
if I drew on my AHSMB unit?

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:44.910
Of course not!

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.950
Those aren't just pictures.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:49.540
Just how stupid are you?

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:54.460
This is Godinion.
Requesting permission for takeoff.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:58.950
This is control.
Godinion is cleared for takeoff.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:01.180
Cleared for takeoff. All ranges: Green.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.340
Increasing backup engine's output.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.310
Activating the turbine's
activation sequence.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.040
All hatches are closed.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.610
External power has been established.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:06.610
AUP activated.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:08.770
Disconnect all equipment.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.630
External pressure increasing.
Turbines activated.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.110
Main engine military!

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:14.150
Blast off!

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:30.080
Th-thanks for all of your hard work.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.640
Same to you!

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.210
All that fighting did a number on it,

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.040
but we've got it working like new!

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.640
Although it's a bit "dressed up" now.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:41.450
Good luck out there! Fight on!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:45.510
Don't sweat it.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:49.780
Ya see, men leave without saying a word
and do their utmost best.

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:53.040
It's okay. You don't
have to say a thing.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.550
Please get on board!

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:55.970
R-right!

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.150
Good luck.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.660
Oh, Boss!

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:00.110
Take care.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:09.150
The interstellar dust around Undina
is denser than elsewhere.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:12.960
It is rich with metals that broke off
from the small, M-class planet.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.730
The space dust can easily interfere
with your radar and communications,

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.040
so be careful.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:22.380
SAIONJI
PHARMACEUTICAL

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.890
Blue 1, ready to go!

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:24.990
Red 5, ready to go!

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.710
Blue 1 and Red 5, I
want you to go first.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:47.870
The team that prevented
Undina Base from

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:51.260
falling has begun setting up the
new transmission satellites.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:56.510
Thanks to your contribution,
we were finally able to sortie.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:01.120
I find that thought pleasing,
yet I am also concerned.

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:04.720
When I think about how they will
be thrown into battle...

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:08.110
That, too, is part of their fate.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:10.620
Even though they are still students,

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.280
they performed wonderfully
in the previous battle.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:15.780
They are associated with the MJP.

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:19.670
The official name is Military
Junior Pre-Academy,

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:22.650
but various news groups are referring
to them as the Majestic Princes.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:25.360
Majestic Princes...

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:27.890
They are unworthy of such a title.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:29.280
That is not true.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:35.210
If it is their fate to fight,
I want them to fight majestically.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.550
Where are Purple 2, Rose 3 and Gold 4?

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.490
They're still undergoing adjustments.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:48.390
Ours won't be fully warmed up in time.

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.430
Gold 4 will be ready for
takeoff momentarily!

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.280
Roger. You'll have to stay
on standby a bit longer.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:00.460
This is what happens when they decide to

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.150
put on a performance
without much warning.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.780
SAIONJI
PHARMACEUTICAL

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.580
Lt. Commander Suzukaze,

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.450
I just received a message from
the broadcast station's staff.

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:13.750
What is it?

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:16.830
They said, "Please wave at the camera."

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.570
From the sponsor's side,

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:21.500
we've received requests to direct their
logos toward the camera

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:22.380
as much as possible.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:26.050
Blue 1, Red 5!

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:29.820
Turn and face the camera so that
the logos are visible and wave?

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:31.110
Seriously?!

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:37.750
Yahoo!

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.900
Let's leave that crud to him.

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:49.490
They're just like Pierrots.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:51.690
In our current situation,
we have no choice

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:54.120
but to rely on those clowns, Lt. Amane.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.690
I am aware of the situation.

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:58.960
What?!

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:00.400
Lt. Commander Suzukaze!

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.840
What? Do they want them to dance next?

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:03.590
It's from HQ.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:06.820
Heat signatures quickly approaching from

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:10.010
Undina Sector  + 32.7 and Sector  151.32.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:16.060
Heat signatures approaching
from your upper right.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:16.850
Keep your eyes peeled.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:18.600
They could be enemy ships!

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.730
Four Wulgaru ships approaching.

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:25.340
Prepare for battle!

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.280
Are there any weapons
you could launch immediately?

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:31.160
Rose 3's main engine will take
another 30 minutes to activate.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:35.030
Purple 2's system could operate
under external electricity.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:38.560
The Red Jaeger and Blue Jaeger's
engines are activating.

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:42.420
It will take seven minutes
for them to warm up.

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:43.810
Can you get out at least one unit?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:44.590
Wait two minutes!

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:47.250
I am forcing the Blue Jaeger to enter
compulsory warm up mode.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.060
And I can also launch Red's HEP Cannon.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.850
Order the news agencies to take shelter.

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:58.070
Prepare to intercept!

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.130
Sound the alarm!

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:09.440
And here I wasn't expecting them
to resume their attack so soon.

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:12.600
Shouldn't we have been
preparing for another

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.110
attack rather than setting up this performance?

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:15.150
Now you say that?

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:17.160
You should have suggested that sooner!

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.510
You're supposed to be my assistant.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.540
I'm terribly sorry.

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.250
I've never seen that unit
in the front before.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:27.630
We don't have any data on it.

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:34.590
They've entered the battlefield.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.110
What should we do?

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:38.640
Um, what should we...?

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:40.900
Keep your wits about
you! Prepare for battle.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:42.360
Wasn't this supposed
to be an easy mission

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.560
where all we did was set up
transmission satellites?

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:45.700
Ow...

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.180
Asagi, are you all right?

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.790
They look just like birds...

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:24.940
They missed?

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:27.900
No, they intentionally didn't hit us.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.110
They're mighty confident...

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.820
We're more likely to
get hit if we move...

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:40.530
How would the JURIA-SYSTEM
respond to the situation?

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:45.160
It isn't doing anything.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:48.750
So we're frozen like frogs
caught in a snake's gaze.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.180
They're totally withering up.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:03.100
Blue Jaegar has completed
its compulsory warm up.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:06.500
Red 5's HEP Cannon is ready for launch.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.330
Blue 1, prepare for linkage!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:12.380
Blue 1, we're increasing your output
to match the enemies' speed.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:14.730
And Red 5, we're launching your weapon.

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:15.490
R-roger!

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.950
We're going to launch
your Assault Jaegar.

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:20.440
Turn on your core's guidance beacon.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.030
Set your controls at half off.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.450
Linkage in a count of five!

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:29.170
Launch!

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:46.730
Linkage connecting in 5, 4, 3, 2, 1!

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:49.650
Now!

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.400
Asagi, you suck on the
actual battlefield...

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:02.450
That wasn't me! My AHSMB
doesn't want to link to it!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.950
Calm down! We're going to try again.

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:08.820
Red 5, we're launching your HEP Cannon!

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:10.990
Kei, operation!

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:14.130
I've input their
acceleration-movement patterns

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.180
and finished calculating 128 patterns
based upon projected Route A.

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:19.190
The most likely route is...

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:23.410
Firing solution ready!
I'm sending it now.

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:54.790
Fire!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:00.590
Did he get them?

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:03.300
They dodged it!

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.990
Linkage: Complete.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:15.970
You took too long.

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:16.780
I'm sorry.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:22.860
They pulled back...?

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:27.700
Don't bother giving chase.

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:29.470
Pull back.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:35.360
<Prince Jiart, are you returning
without finishing the kill?>

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:38.880
<Prey that is easily slain...>

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:42.010
<...is no prey of mine.>

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:51.520
I'm glad you made it back in one piece.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:56.310
But the transmission satellites...

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.860
We were unable to defend them.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:03.030
You see, as much as everyone in the pit

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.040
hates to see machines get destroyed,

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:07.840
we hate it even more when
humans come back in pieces.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:11.540
But I wish you would give your units
a bit more love.

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:15.740
Your DNA is melded into
those AHSMB units.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.460
In a way, they're another
version of yourself.

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:23.970
I'm Reika Saionji, the head mechanic.

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:26.180
But everyone calls me Boss.

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:27.960
Boss...?

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:29.830
She reeks of alcohol.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.320
You're drunk...

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:33.190
I'm on break!

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.710
Please pet my head, too!

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:37.350
Head Mechanic Saionji!

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:40.220
Oh, Rin-Rin! Wanna grab a drink later?

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:41.780
Don't call me that.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:44.940
And I don't want to
drink with a bad drunk.

00:21:47.510 --> 00:21:50.120
Nice work out there. Go
get some rest for now.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.190
Don't worry about a thing.

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:53.550
Got that?

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:01.370
She said not to worry about it!

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:06.520
What're they doing?!

00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:08.590
Aaaaa!
Huh? Something's coming!
He dodged it?!
Chickened out!
Aaaaa!
They suck LOL!

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:55.990
"Surprise Attack"
